
# Orderly 2025 Recap: When Exchange Infrastructure Became Easy to Use
Orderly has been live since 2022, focused on solving the hardest parts of running a perp exchange: you need liquidity to attract traders, but you need traders to attract liquidity.
By the start of 2025, Orderly had already processed $90B supported 34 builders, and served 300k unique wallets.
By the end of 2025, Orderly had now processed $181B and served 893K wallets.
What changed in 2025 was not the technology itself, but who could use it.
For the first time, Orderly’s infrastructure became available with zero code.
From Specialized Infrastructure to a Platform Anyone Can Use
Most infrastructure starts out complicated.
Early on, only advanced teams can use it. Over time, good platforms hide complexity and make powerful tools easier to access.
That is what happened at Orderly.
The early years were spent building the foundation. In 2025, that foundation was opened up as a platform.
This shift brought together governance, vaults, distribution, asset expansion, and a no-code launch pad used by 2058 DEXs, with over 130 that have graduated and are earning fees.
